  "prompt": "A scientist models the efficiency of a biological process using the function\n[Figure 1]\n, where\n[Figure 2]\nrepresents temperature in degrees Celsius,\n[Figure 3]\nrepresents efficiency (in percent), and\n[Figure 4]\nis a positive constant. The model shows that the process has the same efficiency at temperatures of\n[Figure 5]\nand\n[Figure 6]\n. What is the value of\n[Figure 7]\n?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "[Figure 8]",
    "B": "[Figure 9]",
    "C": "[Figure 10]",
    "D": "[Figure 11]"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "C",
  "explanation": "Since $f(3) = f(7)$, the temperatures $3$ and $7$ are symmetric about the axis of symmetry of the parabola. The axis of symmetry is at $x = \\frac{3+7}{2} = 5$. For a quadratic function $f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c$, the axis of symmetry is at $x = -\\frac{b}{2a}$. Here, $-\\frac{k}{2(-2)} = 5$, which simplifies to $\\frac{k}{4} = 5$, giving $k = 20$.",
